{
	title: 'Prompt keys as in the old Hal: delete by words, Alt-D, lost paste',
	description: "Editing keys match the old Hal (questions.md items 35, 37, 41). Alt-Left and Alt-Right move by tokens (a run of letters, digits and _ or a run of punctuation), but Alt-Backspace and Alt-D delete by whitespace words: with 'cat src/host/tools.ts' and the cursor at the end, one Alt-Backspace leaves 'cat '. Alt-D deletes the selection when there is one (not into the kill ring), else kills to the end of the next whitespace word; Ctrl-K and Ctrl-U ignore a selection and drop it. Both the terminal and the web get this through the shared editor step. A bracketed paste whose end marker never arrives is dropped once it has been idle for 5 s, checked on the next input, and that input is read as keys again, so a lost marker cannot swallow the prompt.",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['1x', '9x', 'xk'],
	foldInto: ['1x', '9x', 'xk']
}
